# gx3 two-step remap check

This case copies the gx3 comparison configuration, changing only `npt` from
24 to 2. It uses the B grid and `advection='remap'` and writes to its own
`history/`, `restart/`, and `cice.runlog` paths.

Run `cases/gx3_remap_2step/run.py` with the CUDA-enabled Python environment.
Check `Final calendar: istep=3, npt=2, stop_now=1` and the final lines of
`cice.runlog`. The 24-step Fortran restart cannot be compared with this
two-step run.

On 2026-10-26 the CUDA run completed both steps and printed the expected
final calendar and `CICE COMPLETED SUCCESSFULLY`. Numerical agreement with
Fortran remains untested. The later 24-step case completed successfully;
its retained log is `../gx3_compare/cice.runlog`.
